.TH DRIVERDETECT 8 "October 5, 2026" "RhapsodiOS"
.SH NAME
driverDetect \- list, load and record the drivers for the machine's PCI devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/usr/sbin/driverDetect\fR
.br
\fB/usr/sbin/driverDetect \-l\fR \fIfamily\fR ...
.br
\fB/usr/sbin/driverDetect \-w\fR \fIroot\fR [ \fIdriver\fR ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIdriverDetect\fR reads every PCI function's vendor and device ID
(configuration register 0x00) and subsystem ID (register 0x2c) through the
PCIBus driver's \fBPCI0\fR device, and matches them against the
\fB"Auto Detect IDs"\fR of each PCI driver's \fBDefault.table\fR in
\fB/usr/Devices\fR, with the booter's rules.
.PP
With no arguments it prints one line per match, its fields separated by
tabs: the driver's \fB"Family"\fR, the driver, the device's location and its
ID:
.LP
.DS
Network	NE2K	Dev:3 Func:0 Bus:0	0x802910ec
.DE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fIfamily\fR ...
Load and probe, in the running kernel, the matched drivers whose
\fB"Family"\fR is one of the \fIfamily\fR arguments (Network, SCSI, Disk,
Display, Audio, ...; case does not matter).  Each driver's relocatable is
loaded through kern_loader, then probed with its \fBDefault.table\fR,
\fB"Location"\fR set to the device, held in memory, so nothing is written
to disk.  A driver already loaded when \fIdriverDetect\fR starts is left
alone.  Prints a line, as above, for each device probed.  A network
interface comes up down; \fIifconfig\fR(8) brings it up.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR \fIroot\fR [ \fIdriver\fR ... ]
Record the chosen drivers in the system at \fIroot\fR, normally a disk
being installed.  Each chosen driver must be installed there, in
\fIroot\fB/private/Drivers/i386/\fIdriver\fB.config\fR.  For each device a
chosen driver matches, writes that driver's \fBInstance\fIN\fB.table\fR,
its \fBDefault.table\fR with \fB"Location"\fR and \fB"Instance"\fR filled
in.  Then writes \fIroot\fB/private/Drivers/i386/System.config/Instance0.table\fR
from \fIroot\fB/System/Installation/CDIS/templates/Instance0-i386.table\fR,
or from \fB/System/Installation/CDIS/templates/Instance0-i386.table\fR if
the root has none, with every \fB@DISK@\fR replaced by the disk of the
\fB/\fR line of \fIroot\fB/private/etc/fstab\fR (\fB/dev/hd0a\fR gives
\fBhd0\fR), and:
.RS
.TP
\fB"Boot Drivers"\fR
EISABus PCIBus PS2Keyboard, then each chosen driver whose family is Disk
or SCSI.
.TP
\fB"Active Drivers"\fR
The other chosen drivers, then the template's Active Drivers, less the
chosen ones and less any Network, Display or Audio driver whose family a
chosen driver has.
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exits 0 on success.  Otherwise prints a message on the standard error and
exits 1.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/usr/Devices/\fIdriver\fB.config/Default.table\fR
.TP
\fB/usr/Devices/\fIdriver\fB.config/\fIdriver\fB_reloc\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
driverLoader(8)
